a = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]
index = a.index(5)  #//The index() method is used to find the index of the first occurrence of a specified value in a list. It takes the value to be searched as an argument and returns the index of the first matching element. If the specified value is not found in the list, it raises a ValueError.
print(index)  # Output: 4